                                            "date":  "2026-08-17",
                                            "imageUrl":  null,
                                            "summary":  "With the S\u0026P 500 surging more than 6% in 12 trading days off its late-July lows to fresh record highs, Santoli warns that the earnings quality driving those gains deserves scrutiny. Corporate profits are tracking toward 30% year-over-year growth in 2026, aided by nominal GDP running above 6% and roughly $750 billion in AI capex flowing through the economy Ã¢â‚¬â€ but results are being flattered by paper gains as tech giants mark up their AI equity stakes, by data-center revenue being recognized ahead of associated future expenses, and by a one-time energy-sector earnings surge tied to wartime supply disruptions.",
                                            "take":  "This is a crucial quality-of-earnings warning at a moment when headline profit growth figures are being used to justify elevated valuations. When earnings beats are partly a function of mark-to-market gains on AI investments and front-loaded revenue recognition, the multiple the market is paying on \u0027real\u0027 normalized earnings is meaningfully higher than the reported P/E suggests. Investors should be asking whether 2026\u0027s 30% EPS growth is a repeatable baseline or a one-cycle phenomenon before extrapolating current valuations forward.",
